From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:29:46 -0400
Subject: spaces: a chip drag reorders the switcher; splits: a split's panes
 take a Space, a pin and a sleep together

A Space chip dragged along the switcher row lands on the nearest chip's
place (SwitcherDropIndex) and the model moves the Space a turn later, since
the move rebuilds the row that holds the dragged chip (docs/features/
spaces.md B27). A split's panes are one row: SpaceModel::SetSpaceForTab and
SetSpacePinned reach both panes through SplitPeers, a pinned split stays
where it is, and the selection already carries both panes for Sleep
(docs/features/splits.md J4). The floating Space name is dropped when a
menu opens on a chip or the row is rebuilt, since the chip never sees the
pointer leave in either case.

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-18 B27, R6-19 J4), the last rows of
the wave.
Removable when: Chromium's tab strip hosts a Space switcher with drag
reorder and treats a split as one unit for membership and pins.
